title: 'Registrar: set current head'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Implements `set_current_head` in the registrar. Root, the para itself, or its manager while
    the para is unlocked can call it on `pallet-registrar-para` (CT in Polkadot, AH in Kusama). The
    parachain checks that the para is registered and that the head fits `MaxHeadDataSize`, then
    sends `SetCurrentHead` to the relay chain. Nothing is stored on the parachain, since setting a
    head holds no deposit and can simply be asked again.

    On the relay chain, `pallet-registrar-relay` checks that the para is still registered and that
    the head fits the live `max_head_data_size`, sets it through `paras_registrar` and reports
    back. A para the relay chain no longer knows, e.g. after a deregistration overtook the request,
    is refused with the new `FailureReason::NotRegistered`, and a head that is too large with the
    new `FailureReason::HeadDataTooLarge`. The parachain surfaces the answer as `HeadUpdated` or
    `HeadUpdateFailed`.
crates:
- name: registrar-primitives
  bump: major
- name: pallet-registrar-para
  bump: major
- name: pallet-registrar-relay
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-runtime-common
  bump: patch
